STATEFULSET
->in k8s for app running we are using deployment, fr database we are using statefulset
IQ- can we run db's using deployment?
no
->we have 2 types of app's in k8s
1)stateless = no past data is saved
2)stateful = stores  data forever
->for stateless app's we use deployment nd for stateful we use staefulset
IQ - diff b/w deployment n statefulset?
deployment
->pods names are random
->pods dels randomly
statefulset
->pod names in sequential(flm0 flm1 flm2)
->pods del last created(last in first out)
IQ - why we are using statefulset for db's?
deployment lo 2 pods unnai scaling tho increase chesthey at a tym cretae avutai, ade statefulset one by one by cloning the data frm prev pod data
take img at 18mins
NOTE -1 db ni deployment tho create chesamu(a db only oka data undi pod create chesetapudu,customer 2nd tym add chesadu data), now we scaled app and increased pods 2nd pod lo only oka customer data ney vastadi
2 thats the drawback of deployment
3 ade manam statefulset use chesthey prev data clone avutadi - so use staefulset fr db's
->write manifest file fr deployment, observe pods are creating at a time
->write manifest file fr statefulset, observe pods creates sequentially
NOTE - manifest file is same fr statefulset as deployment only kind is diff

DAEMONSETS
->monitoring, logging ki use chestamu
->suppose hyb city lo diff ganges untaru like theives, smuggling, mafia untai
-> so ee ganges lo em jarugutundi ani teliyali antey secret ga prathi gang lo oka person ni inject chestaru
->a persons chusthu untaru em jarugutundi prathi team lo ani
->likewise mana cluster lo prathi pod lo em jarugutundi (cpu-utilization,pod running lo undha leda, ey worker-node ekkuva mem consume chestundi)
->so mana cluster lo prathi worker-node lo oka pod ni create chestamu so ee pods mem usage, cpu-utilization, pod health anni gather chesi monitoring dashboards ki send chestai
->active ga monitor chestadi ee daemonset prathi worker node lo unna damenonset pod
->manifest file is same as statefulset only kind will vary nd replicas koda undavu
->present mana cluster lo one-master, 2-nodes. manaki cluster size saripola, so we increased one-more node then daemonset will automatically created
NOTE -1  manam cluster ki oka cmd run cheska, cluster creation ki oka cmd vastadi dani tho patu inka konni cmds vastai, avi save chesi unchuko
2 those cmds will help in changing the cluster size/modifications
